2182:LOGBOOK.md:14:- FINDING (missing from the entry below, which stopped at `7a66c73`): the deeper CocoaSkills defect was never Windows-specific. `_validate_namespace_independence` compared every namespace with every other and canonicalised **both** operands per comparison, and the pass re-runs on every journal save — **twice per 32 KiB staging chunk**. One install measured **750,620** canonicalisations, 182 s of its 210 s, *on macOS*. Windows opens a handle per path component for the same question, so only there did quadratic-with-a-cheap-constant become fatal. A POSIX-latent cost defect that a slower syscall promotes to an outage is worth looking for before the next change near a hot revalidation path.
