2250:LOGBOOK.md:1923:- DECISION: renamed the descriptor family only (`curator-build.json`, `curator-build-v1{,.schema.json}`, `curatorBuildTargetV1`, two generator helpers); left the digest-algorithm namespace untouched. All nine rc.4 frozen digests re-verified unchanged.
2251:LOGBOOK.md:1925:- FINDING: the descriptor path is part of the external build input, so the rename is a real cache-identity revision, not cosmetic. External `go-repository-v1` cache key `07dd911a…` → `4abc903b…`, external receipt hash `11d2bf4d…` → `0f8f910a…`. Local `go-v1` carries no descriptor and is byte-identical (`1a887eb6…`), which is what scopes the change to the external driver.
2252:LOGBOOK.md:1926:- SCOPE: `curator-spec` @ `57c1f56` + rc.5 candidate; 71 files, one schema file and one schema-case directory renamed. New candidate pin `sha256:9ba9b8ec…`.
2253:LOGBOOK.md:1946:- NOTE: the fix deletes the window it closes, so no permanent install-level test can hook "between the digest and the read". The invariant is locked at the read instead, with a one-shot `afterDocumentOpen` seam (nil in production, same convention as `godriver.controlSeamFault`), and the negative control runs **both** orderings: digest-before-read fails all four install-level ABA cases *by committing the transient declaration*, digest-after-read fails the rename binding case. The byte-identical-rewrite control passes in every variant, so the cases are not merely restart-happy.
2254:LOGBOOK.md:2107:- ANOMALY: first native Windows full-suite run exposed pre-existing gaps in packages this task does not own — `buildcache` (`owner does not match the effective user` on temp roots), `buildsource` (Windows rename/path semantics), `globalbins` and `runtimestore` (`script command is not executable`, POSIX exec-bit assumption), `shell` (PowerShell hook). All pass on both macOS hosts. Reported, not fixed.
2255:LOGBOOK.md:2144:- FINDING: `quarantinePath` now faults and syncs after the compensating rename restores the live slot. A second sync failure preserves the exact live bytes but becomes a key-bearing `StateChangedError`; a successful second sync keeps the ordinary compensated-error contract.
2256:LOGBOOK.md:2152:- TRUST BOUNDARY: the preserved legacy and scoped traversals match on canonical record order/content, SHA-256 identity, diagnostic code and detail across paths, symlinks, error precedence, cancellation, directory/file/ancestor replacement, an in-root replacement link, and rename-away/rename-back ABA. Both earlier detached-directory and listed-directory reclassification regressions pass.
