2274:LOGBOOK.md:2300:- DARWIN FINDING: Darwin rejects directory rename when the source directory lacks owner write permission, including sealed `0500` state. Locked quarantine now reserves a unique target, grants owner control only through verified no-follow state, atomically moves the candidate, and restores its prior mode in quarantine; `0700`, `0550`, `0000`, and sealed `0500` cases pass.
2275:LOGBOOK.md:2305:- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` on the unchanged CocoaSkills candidate rooted at `97a0ed870782b48eebc5a9c25a9cfa8fea5ff245`; no product source or test file was modified.
2276:LOGBOOK.md:2312:- TRIGGER: CocoaSkills PR #11 CI run `30514706010` passed strict mypy plus every macOS and Windows test job, but all four Ubuntu versions failed the same four cache tests at `_move_aside` with `PermissionError: [Errno 13]`.
2277:LOGBOOK.md:2313:- ROOT CAUSE: the verified temporary owner-unlock path was gated to Darwin. Linux therefore attempted ordinary quarantine rename with sealed directory modes `0500`, `0550`, or `0000`; owner write/execute control was absent at the rename boundary.
2278:LOGBOOK.md:2314:- FIX: the existing rooted, no-follow, effective-UID and inode-verified unlock now applies to owned POSIX directories generally, skips mutation only when full owner `rwx` is already present, and restores the exact original mode after both successful and failed rename.
2279:LOGBOOK.md:2315:- REGRESSION: Linux-semantic seams force `EACCES` unless the candidate has temporary owner control, cover sealed `0500`, untrusted `0550`, and inaccessible `0000`, and prove exact mode restoration plus reservation cleanup when rename itself fails.
2280:LOGBOOK.md:2320:- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` cycle 3 on CocoaSkills base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`; clean local `main`, `main`, and `origin/main` matched, both dependency tasks were accepted, and the four candidate hashes matched the producer packet. No CocoaSkills source or test file was modified.
2281:LOGBOOK.md:2335:- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` retained the published CocoaSkills task branch at HEAD `0d6ad16fce35c1bd8854511e13766cd236908e3b` and base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`. The final unstaged product delta contains only `cache_posix.py` and its focused tests; `cache.py` matches HEAD and no `uv.lock` remains.
2282:LOGBOOK.md:2337:- FAILURE SAFETY: unlock now occurs before destination reservation. Original mode is restored and reservations are removed across fsync, reopen, rename, retry, unsupported-capability, and cleanup failures. Tests cover sealed `0500`, untrusted `0550`, inaccessible `0000`, exact restoration, and zero reservation leakage.
2283:LOGBOOK.md:2350:- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` retained the CocoaSkills task branch at HEAD `0d6ad16fce35c1bd8854511e13766cd236908e3b` and base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`. The unstaged product delta remains exactly `cache_posix.py` and its focused tests; `cache.py` matches HEAD.
2284:LOGBOOK.md:2351:- RACE CLOSED: publication now retains the rooted no-follow staged-directory descriptor across atomic rename and seals only that exact inode. If another publisher moves it during the private-mode seal window, the first publisher never seals or quarantines the replacement by logical name; it opens the selected live winner read-only and compares pinned canonical receipt and artifact bytes.
2285:LOGBOOK.md:2352:- DETERMINISTIC PROOF: publisher A is paused after rename until publisher B exceeds the retry window, quarantines A, publishes and seals a different inode, and returns. Identical bytes yield B=`published`, A=`reused-winner`; different bytes yield B=`published`, A=`CacheConflictError`. Both schedules leave a protected live hit, a sealed quarantined loser, and empty staging.
