111099-+## Why error 87 does not identify a native status
111100-+
111101-+Microsoft defines [`ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER` as 87](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/system-error-codes--0-499-).
111102:+[`RtlNtStatusToDosError`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winternl/nf-winternl-rtlntstatustodoserror)
111103-+maps NTSTATUS to a Win32 system error and explicitly documents that there is no
111104-+inverse function. Therefore the Win32 result cannot prove whether the wrapper
111105-+rejected the record before a syscall or translated one of multiple native
--
111115-+does not itself explain these runs.
