124579-+## Why error 87 does not identify a native status
124580-+
124581-+Microsoft defines [`ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER` as 87](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/system-error-codes--0-499-).
124582:+[`RtlNtStatusToDosError`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winternl/nf-winternl-rtlntstatustodoserror)
124583-+maps NTSTATUS to a Win32 system error and explicitly documents that there is no
124584-+inverse function. Therefore the Win32 result cannot prove whether the wrapper
124585-+rejected the record before a syscall or translated one of multiple native
--
124595-+does not itself explain these runs.
124596-+
124597-+The native patch is diagnostically better as well as identity-safe:
124598:+[`NtSetInformationFile`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/drivers/ddi/ntifs/nf-ntifs-ntsetinformationfile)
124599-+returns the raw status, takes an `IO_STATUS_BLOCK`, documents class 10 and its
124600-+`DELETE` requirement, and explicitly instructs user-mode callers to use the
124601:+`NtSetInformationFile` name.
