{"commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T19:05:56Z","email":"6414091+MatejKafka@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matěj Kafka"},"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T19:05:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Clarify FILE_RENAME_INFO RootDirectory and FileNameLength fields (#1123)\n\n- RootDirectory: Can be a directory handle for relative name resolution,\n  not just NULL. Clarify the common case vs the relative-name use case.\n- FileNameLength: Clarify that a terminating null is not required.\n\nCo-authored-by: John Kennedy \u003cjohn_kenn@mac.com\u003e\nCo-authored-by: MatejKafka \u003c64140091+MatejKafka@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e"},"files":[{"additions":2,"changes":4,"deletions":2,"filename":"sdk-api-src/content/winbase/ns-winbase-file_rename_info.md","patch":"@@ -73,11 +73,11 @@ This field is used when **SetFileInformationByHandle**'s *FileInformationClass*\n \n ### -field RootDirectory\n \n-This field should be set to NULL.\n+Set to **NULL** in the common case. If **FileName** specifies a relative name, this field can be a handle to the directory relative to which the new name is resolved.\n \n ### -field FileNameLength\n \n-The size of **FileName** in bytes, not including the NUL-termination.\n+The size of **FileName** in bytes. A terminating null character is not required.\n \n ### -field FileName\n ","status":"modified"}],"sha":"d1debc569f40cda761474d216903f27c8aa7c7af"}

